WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.781
Hi, how are you?
(audience applauding)

2
00:00:01.781 --> 00:00:04.190
Hi! Oh my goodness.

3
00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:06.700
I'm so excited to be speaking with you.

4
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.830
It's an honor to be in the whole "Scream" franchise,

5
00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:10.663
with you.

6
00:00:10.663 --> 00:00:11.970
Whoa. Okay, wait.

7
00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.480 line:15%
One, thank you. Two, I know.

8
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.410 line:15%
I was freaking out,

9
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.670 line:15%
because the "Scream" cast and directors,

10
00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:18.530 line:15%
we have this group chat,

11
00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.100
and we all still talk to each other,

12
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:20.933
so, I told them.

13
00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:22.300
I was like, "Guys, I'm talking with Drew,

14
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.230
should I just spoil the whole film?"

15
00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.547
And one of the directors, Matt, told me,

16
00:00:25.547 --> 00:00:27.320
"Oh yeah, I can send you the whole cut right now,

17
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.455
and she could put it on your show."

18
00:00:28.455 --> 00:00:30.790
(audience chuckling)
Well...

19
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:31.623
No, you have no idea, like,

20
00:00:31.623 --> 00:00:34.150
how excited I am to be speaking with you,

21
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.760
how much we praise your film.

22
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.895
I remember on Halloween, even, we went on our set,

23
00:00:38.895 --> 00:00:41.660
we set up a projector and we got popcorn,

24
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.990
and watching the original, like,

25
00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.430
I cannot tell you how many times

26
00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:47.670
I have seen your opening scene.

27
00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:52.640
I am so honored to be a part of this franchise with you.

28
00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.500
And by the way,

29
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.946
I only made it this far in the book last night, but I just,

30
00:00:56.946 --> 00:00:57.870
(paper rustling)
I can't tell you.

31
00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.900
The whole thing is circled, and annotated,

32
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.690
page after page after page.

33
00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.513
It's so beautiful.

34
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.433
Thank you.

35
00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:10.060
What inspired you to write this book?

36
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.570
Just growing up in this day and age,

37
00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:15.150
where social media can be so harmful and so toxic

38
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.520
to young people's mental health, or even older people,

39
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.280
I think it's really important to know,

40
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.400
that people that you see on the screen,

41
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.390
or people that, you know, you may support,

42
00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:25.930
go through the same things that you do,

43
00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:29.100
and we all kind of struggle with self-esteem or self-love,

44
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.710
and it's a tough journey to get there.

45
00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.190
And I think that with this book,

46
00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.850
I really just wanted to reach out to people

47
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:35.830
who may also be struggling,

48
00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:38.000
or people who just wanted to get to know myself

49
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:38.833
a little bit better,

50
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:40.400
and that's why there's so many intimate stories,

51
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.310
or embarrassing stories, or mistakes that I've made,

52
00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.810
that people may or may not learn from.

53
00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.190
You have the wisdom of someone

54
00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.920
who's lived an entire life cycle,

55
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.160
and you know,

56
00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.970
where do you think you learned, for example,

57
00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.640
like, when, you know, you love someone,

58
00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.630
maybe don't keep the mementos.

59
00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.860
Can you speak to that? I loved that.

60
00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:05.000 line:15%
I know for me, personally, I live in the past a lot.

61
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.220 line:15%
And I think that sometimes that kind of stops

62
00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.060 line:15%
or halts my growth as a person,

63
00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.210
because I'm so stuck at what happened in the past,

64
00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.790
or things that I'm embarrassed of,

65
00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:15.300
or mistakes that I've made,

66
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.060 line:15%
that I don't appreciate the present time that I'm in,

67
00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:23.090 line:15%
or I am so stuck on that, that I just can't move forward.

68
00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:25.033
I mean, mementos tend to be memories of the good times,

69
00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.500 line:15%
and not of the bad times,

70
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:29.950 line:15%
so, if you're only holding on to these amazing pieces,

71
00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.540 line:15%
or pieces that made you smile,

72
00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.090 line:15%
or when you think about this person,

73
00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.700 line:15%
or friend, or whoever it may be,

74
00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.630 line:15%
I think it is just kind of holding you back in a sense.

75
00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:39.463 line:15%
And I know for me,

76
00:02:39.463 --> 00:02:42.510 line:15%
I'm trying to live a bit of a more minimalist lifestyle.

77
00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.220
So, I try to keep things as plain and simple

78
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.320
as I possibly can be,

79
00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.080
especially with how crowded my brain can be sometimes.

80
00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.280
And again, those mementos,

81
00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:50.820
they just kind of crowd your thoughts,

82
00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.760
and kind of fog your memory, in a sense, I think.

83
00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.870
You also talk about the difference between love

84
00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:56.810
and infatuation.

85
00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:57.973
Will you speak to that?

86
00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.360
Yeah.

87
00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:01.740
Again, social media,

88
00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.510 line:15%
it's so easy for people to portray this perfect, clean,

89
00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:06.550 line:15%
beautiful lifestyle,

90
00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:09.870 line:15%
that I really think that social media people just post,

91
00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.500 line:15%
and appear how how they want to be,

92
00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.120 line:15%
rather than they truly are.

93
00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.540 line:15%
People who haven't experienced love before,

94
00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.470 line:15%
this infatuation, this crush that they start to develop,

95
00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:19.030 line:15%
it could feel like true love.

96
00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:20.120 line:15%
And when they meet that person,

97
00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.360 line:15%
or start to interact with that person,

98
00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.590 line:15%
and realize that they're not as perfect

99
00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.890
as their mind had made them out to be,

100
00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.130
I think you could be disappointed,

101
00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:32.270
and it's unfair to that other person to be disappointed,

102
00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.480
because of the expectations that you created,

103
00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.523
in your own head.

104
00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:37.203
I just,

105
00:03:37.203 --> 00:03:39.700
I don't think that we should take social media so seriously

106
00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.533
and so deeply,

107
00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:45.010
and create these ideas about somebody,

108
00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:49.050
who truly is just trying to appear cool, or, you know,

109
00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.190
be well-liked or popular or whatever it may be.

110
00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:53.890
Whatever they're trying to achieve on Instagram.

111
00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.800
You have so much to offer.

112
00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.700
You are such a gift, Jenna Ortega.

113
00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:00.533
Everybody,

114
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:03.460
"It's All Love, Reflections for your Heart and Soul",

115
00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:05.930
is available right now.

116
00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.410
Jenna Ortega, it is such a pleasure to get to know you,

117
00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.700
and please, I would love to see you again.

118
00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:13.560
Thank you, it's an honor.

119
00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.227 line:15%
(upbeat music)

